<title>
Adaptive Cruise Control System Symptom Diagnosis
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Adaptive cruise control system is controlled by the RBS control module communicating with ESP<sup>®</sup> control module, BCM, ECM, TCM (A/T model), lighting and turn signal switch, dual sensor brake support control module and combination meter through CAN communication. Before performing symptom diagnosis, check that no DTC is indicated in these control modules.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<diag type = "condition" id = "AENLSB0AA124010001">
<condition>
<ptxt>
Adaptive cruise control system cannot be ON
</ptxt>
</condition>
<ps>
<ptxt>
Faulty CRUISE (main) switch
</ptxt>
</ps>
<action>
<ptxt>
Check CRUISE (main) switch. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0AA126003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</action>
<ps>
